course: dictionary
lesson: 6757
title: Opaque: light cannot get through
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Opaque describes a material that light cannot pass through, so you cannot see through it. «Transparent materials let light through, translucent ones let some through, and opaque ones block it.» The clue is the word block: if something blocks light, you cannot see through it.
explain: The sentences show what opaque looks like in use. «A shadow forms where an opaque object blocks the light.» Behind an opaque object, no light gets through, so a dark area forms. Wood is opaque: «Materials that let none through, like wood, are opaque.»
explain: Opaque can also mean hard to understand, not clear, when used about words or ideas. Check by swapping your meaning in. For light, "no light gets through" fits the sentence. For an idea, "hard to see into and understand" fits too.
fact: Opaque means light cannot pass through, so you cannot see through it.
fact: Opaque materials, like wood and cardboard, make shadows.
fact: «Transparent» means clear, like glass; «translucent» means some light gets through, like tracing paper.
fact: Opaque can also mean hard to understand or not clear, used about words or ideas.
fact: Opaque tights and opaque curtains stop you seeing through them.
exercise: «Materials that let none through, like wood, are opaque.» What does opaque mean here? | Light makes it glow | *Light cannot pass through | It is very heavy | Light passes straight through
exercise: «A shadow forms where an opaque object blocks the light.» What makes a shadow? | A cold wind | Light passing through clear glass | Lots of light shining everywhere | *An object that blocks the light
exercise: Which material is opaque? | *Cardboard | Tracing paper | Frosted glass | Clear glass
test: «Her explanation was opaque, and I could not follow it.» What does opaque mean here? | Made of glass | *Hard to understand, not clear | Very bright | Clear and easy to follow
test: Which word means some light gets through? | Solid | Opaque | *Translucent | Shadow
exam: Which object would make a room the darkest when placed in front of a window? | *A thick wooden door | Tracing paper | Clear glass | Frosted glass
